{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/64246-darkening-sky-errata","id":64246,"title":"Darkening Sky errata","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-03T13:05:42-08:00","id":64246,"title":"Darkening Sky errata","content":"If you've found any typos or visual errors in <i>Darkening Sky</i>, post them here. Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T14:04:40-08:00","id":64301,"title":"","content":"Hi,<br /> I have found a few, some can be argued if they are typos or deliberate:<br /> <br /> The term Kindred is used for Cainites on many pages in the book. Please switch to Cainite/s. (The term Kindred is not used for the Cainite race until the 1400s, and does not appear AFAIK in any of the other 55+ products in the Dark Ages line).<br /> <br /> Gerushah bint Yoav's embrace date, generation and clan differs from Veil of Night, page 96. (Brujah, 7th gen, Embrace 854 CE) This contradicts established canon, for no apparent reason. In both however, she is Sultan of Sevilla and of jewish heritage and has converted to Islam.<br /> <br /> The term Crimson Curia is used in the Cainite Heresy book as the clerical body of the Heresy. This seem to contradict the description of the Crimson Curia in Darkening Sky, page 102, where Crimson Curia is synonymous with the Shadow Reconquista. Even, on page 92, the Cainite Heresy and Crimson Curia are identified as two separate entities with church ties. This contradicts established canon.<br /> <br /> <br /> On page 95, Alfonso de Landa is having his allegience stated in the name &quot;Crimson Curia: Alfonso de Landa&quot;. Of the 9 listed NPC's in this section, he is the only one using this format. All NPC's should use same format, IMHO.<br /> <br /> <br /> /Ho Dracon<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/390-ho-dracon","name":"Ho Dracon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar390_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T14:21:29-08:00","id":64308,"title":"","content":"P. 43: &quot;<b>Given Even</b> if the Spring Court does not come out on top...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T03:50:57-08:00","id":65541,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#050505\">In the text, the spirit is spelled Da\u017ebog, but on each header (pages 21 &amp; 36), it\u2019s spelled D\u01cezbog. In the index, page 3, there\u2019s no accent mark at all (Dazbog).<br /> <br /> Also, on page 38, it\u2019s not indicated what type of Rite the </span>Rite of the Silken Cloth is. I assume it\u2019s Mystic.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=